From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:28:23 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: MACRUNNER_FEX_HOOK_GUARD - compile and
 code-buffer-change paths (HG2, on top of HG1)

Same class as HG1, other lock mode: CompileBlock / CompileSingleStep hold CodeInvalidationMutex SHARED, and inside them the FEX allocator frees/allocates memory
(end-of-compile locals: DebugData, CodePages, IR; JIT.cpp:1125 CTX->ClearCodeCache -> SharedCodeBufferManager::AllocateNew/~CodeBuffer = VirtualAlloc/VirtualFree).
A NotifyMemory* hook fired by that then asks for the EXCLUSIVE mutex under the thread's own shared one (upgrade) - the same self-deadlock. Candidate for the
ER-CODEBUF hang (MACRUNNER_FEX_CODEBUF_MAX=1).

FEXCore cannot see the Windows HookGuard, so SyscallHandler gets EnterRuntimeSection/LeaveRuntimeSection (Compile, ClearCodeCache; no-ops by default) like PreCompile;
Core.cpp raises them right after the shared lock in CompileBlock/CompileSingleStep and at the start of ClearCodeCache. The ARM64EC and WOW64 handlers map them to
HookGuard::Enter/Leave. The per-thread depth becomes three bytes (invalidation, compile, code-buffer change) so the counters can be split by path:
hg_scopes_inv/compile/clear (scope entries) and hs_path_inv/compile/clear (suppressed notifications attributed to the innermost path). Same gate as HG1.
